<h1>Monk::Live demo</h1>
<p>
  Open this page in two tabs and press the button in one: the counter in the
  other updates by itself. The server pushes the new HTML over a WebSocket;
  there is no polling and no page JavaScript of your own.
</p>

<%# live_topic makes this element's page subscribe to the "demo:hits" topic. %>
<p <%= live_topic "demo:hits" %>>Hits so far: <%= render "demo/_hits", hits: locals[:hits], layout: false %></p>

<form method="post" action="/demo/live/hit"><button>+1</button></form>

<p>
  The pieces: <code>live_topic</code> in this view, the partial
  <code>app/views/demo/_hits.erb</code>, <code>Monk::Live.patch</code> in
  <code>POST /demo/live/hit</code> (<code>app/routes/demo_live.rb</code>), and
  the subscribe rule in <code>config/live.rb</code>.
</p>
